From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:38:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/28] Pinned offline build closure for the verifier runtime's
 binaries; document it

scripts/rpc-runtime/closure.json pins the three native sources by commit and tree (Helios aca81764,
listener 5e178676), the base/base 5476069f tarball by sha256, Rust 1.96.0 and both Cargo.locks.
build-binaries.sh exports exact trees with git archive, extracts base/base from the verified tarball
into the relative path Helios names (vendor-inspect/base-v1.5.1, so no unrecorded local tree is
read), builds --locked --offline with remapped paths and checks neither lock nor the listener's
generated manifest changed. cargo-home-from-lock.py assembles a CARGO_HOME holding exactly the
locked crates (each checked against the lock's checksum; the one git dependency by commit).

Release builds under the 1536 MiB guard: listener 9ca75047 and witness-check a3377048 built and are
added to PINNED_BUILDS; the Helios release build was stopped by the guard at 1547 MiB and was not
retried, so the tested Helios stays the debug build cc962e2b. docs/network/local-chain-verifier.md:
order, config, build and run, systemd sketch, consumer opt-in, activation and rollback, and what
the runtime does not do (finality, provider independence, public serving, Windows).
